// XFAIL: RT-483: UNSOUND: `&mut x` of a parameter not declared `mut` (`fn w(x: i64)`) is accepted and writes it: the program prints 6; rustc E0596 (cannot borrow `x` as mutable, as it is not declared as mutable). A `let x` local is refused right (0.30.2)
// From the re-review of the fn-value work (g302fnval). Since v0.30.1 at least.
